From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: add the ADSP
 sleep-state entries

The stock iceland DT gives the ADSP's SMP2P edge two more entries, an
outbound "sleepstate" (the AP-awake bit) and an inbound "sleepstate_see"
(the sensor engine), and a qcom,smp2p-sleepstate node that ties them to
the sleep-state notifier. Mainline lacks all three, so the ADSP and its
sensor hub are never told that Linux suspends.

Add the entries and the consumer node as the stock DT has them. The
inbound interrupt is requested on both edges, like the stock driver.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts    | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index be9c4112fe6a..4688d399057a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -3882,3 +3882,31 @@ map1 {
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * The sleep-state entries of the ADSP's SMP2P edge, as in the stock DT:
+ * Linux clears the AP-awake bit of "sleepstate" before system suspend and
+ * sets it again after resume; "sleepstate_see" is the inbound entry of the
+ * sensor engine (SEE) on the ADSP.
+ */
+&{/smp2p-adsp} {
+	smp2p_adsp_sleepstate_out: sleepstate-out {
+		qcom,entry-name = "sleepstate";
+		#qcom,smem-state-cells = <1>;
+	};
+
+	smp2p_adsp_sleepstate_in: sleepstate-in {
+		qcom,entry-name = "sleepstate_see";
+		interrupt-controller;
+		#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+	};
+};
+
+/ {
+	smp2p-sleepstate {
+		compatible = "qcom,smp2p-sleepstate";
+		qcom,smem-states = <&smp2p_adsp_sleepstate_out 0>;
+		interrupts-extended = <&smp2p_adsp_sleepstate_in 0 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_BOTH>;
+		interrupt-names = "smp2p-sleepstate-in";
+	};
+};
